## Introduction

This is the dataset of DFT-PBEsol data in CeO$_2$-ZrO$_2$ ceramics for training DeepMD model. Type 1, 2, and 3 are O, Zr, and Ce respectively. The users can refer to Ref. [1] for details. An example of INCAR is shown in Supplementary Material of Ref. [1].

## General Approach

The DFT dataset was prepared using a concurrent-learning scheme implemented in DP-GEN (Deep Generator) [2]. The DP-GEN software iteratively explores the configurational space through three steps: training, exploration, and labelling. In the training step, DP-GEN invokes the DeePMD-kit package to train four DP models with different activation functions based on an initial DFT dataset. The initial training dataset incorporates structures of pure ZrO$_2$ and CeO$_2$-ZrO$_2$ solid solutions. Notably, DFT data from a prior study [3] on DP-ZrO$_2$-PBEsol—which demonstrated accuracy comparable to DFT for phase transformations—were included in the initial CeO$_2$-ZrO$_2$ training dataset. Besides that, various ZrO$_2$ structures comprising 96 atoms (monoclinic, tetragonal, cubic, Pbc2$_1$, Pbca, and liquid phases) were generated by molecular dynamics utilizing the DP-ZrO$_2$-PBEsol model. Subsequently, in these structures, 1 to 8, 10, 12, 16, 20, 25, and 32 Zr atoms were randomly substituted with Ce atoms to encompass the entire compositional spectrum. The cell parameters of the resultant CeO$_2$-ZrO$_2$ structures were re-scaled based on the compositions and lattice parameters of c-ZrO$_2$ and c-CeO$_2$. Additionally, low-index surfaces of monoclinic and tetragonal CeO$_2$-ZrO$_2$ phases were similarly generated and included. Overall, the initial training dataset, used to train the four initial CeO$_2$-ZrO$_2$ DP models, comprised 1,160 CeO$_2$-ZrO$_2$ and 5,057 ZrO$_2$ structures.

During the exploration stage, DP-GEN uses LAMMPS [4] to conduct hybrid molecular dynamics/Monte Carlo simulations for CeO$_2$-ZrO$_2$ systems across various phases, compositions, pressures, and temperatures, thereby extensively probing the configurational space. The phases and composition spectrum are consistent with those of CeO$_2$-ZrO$_2$ structures in the initial training dataset. Temperatures were progressively raised from 100 K to 4500 K over the course of the DP-GEN iterations, exploring pressures ranging from -5 to 20 GPa. The low-index surfaces of CeO$_2$-ZrO$_2$ monoclinic and tetragonal phases below 500 K were also generated in this step. To efficiently evaluate the predictive accuracy of the DP models trained in the preceding step, we measured the prediction deviations among DP models using model deviations, defined as the maximum standard deviation in predicted atomic forces across different DP models. Large model deviations highlight the low predictive accuracy for the generated structures, underscoring the need for training dataset refinement. In the present study, the configurations with model deviations from 0.20 eV/Å to 0.40 eV/Å were randomly added into the training dataset. For liquid structures, the range is adjusted to 0.30-0.50 eV/Å. The upper limit of model deviations is set to avoid picking up potential unphysical configurations.

In the labeling phase, the energy, atomic forces, and stresses of the chosen configurations were computed using the Vienna ab initio simulation package (VASP) [5,6], employing the Perdew-Burke-Ernzerhof exchange-correlation functional revised for solids (PBEsol) [7], which is denoted as DFT-PBEsol below. The calculations were set with a plane-wave cutoff of 900 eV and a 3×3×3 Monkhorst-Pack k-mesh to ensure convergence of the energies, atomic forces, and virials for the distorted crystals and liquid configurations of CeO$_2$-ZrO$_2$ systems. To accelerate the DFT calculations, a sequential two-step strategy is implemented. In the first step, wavefunctions of electrons are brought to a preliminary level of convergence rapidly with reduced precision, facilitated by enabling specific computational efficiency settings in VASP (see Supplementary Materials in Ref. [1] for details). Following this, the calculation is advanced to a high precision, commencing from the initially preconverged wavefunctions. This approach effectively reduces the overall computational time while maintaining  accuracy of the results. A total of 12,303 configurations have been incorporated into the DFT-PBEsol dataset.

